{"type":"message","id":"936fbe96","parentId":"c1a2dae5","timestamp":"2026-05-17T19:04:29.451Z","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"text","text":"[Sun 2026-05-17 19:01 UTC] Write a dream diary entry from these memory fragments:\n\n- Assistant: **TLSNotary** | ❌ 不需要 | ⚠️ 部分 | ❌ 仅数据 | ✅ 中等 | 链下服务信任 | --- ## ⚠️ 暗坑：TEE 的\"硬件信任\"并非万能 主公若在考虑从 TEE 转向替代方案，有一事不得不察： **TEE 最脆弱的地方恰恰就是它的卖点** — 对硬件厂商的信任。Intel SGX 已被多次攻破（Plundervolt、Smash、AEPIC Leak），而且 Intel 停用了 SGX 的远程证明服务。AMD SEV 也有 side-channel 漏洞。硬件 TEE 的安全边界并不像宣传的那么绝对。\n- Assistant: **建议**：主公若只是想跟几个合作企业共享一个自用应用，路径 B 最轻量。若未来打算做 SaaS 产品面向所有企业卖，再走 ISV 路径。 需要我进一步拆解某个环节的具体操作吗？比如如何配置事件订阅，或者如何获取外部用户 open_id？\n- Assistant: 3：冷启动延迟 TDX VM 启动 + Attestation → 约 5-15 秒。 用户等一个 Skill 执行需要 5 秒冷启动，体验不行。 **解决方案：预启动 TDX Pool** ``` 始终维持 N 个已 Attest 的 TDX VM ↓ 用户请求 → 分配一个空闲 VM → 注入 Skill → 执行 ↓ 冷启动 < 500ms（VM 已在池中） ``` --- ## 四、给创作者的实际开发流程设计 假设方案确定为 **WASM in TDX**： ``` 1. echo dev init # 初始化 Skill"}],"timestamp":1779044669355}}
{"type":"message","id":"f94a2151","parentId":"936fbe96","timestamp":"2026-05-17T19:04:40.348Z","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"The user wants me to write a dream diary entry in first person, drawing from the memory fragments provided about TLSNotary, TEE (Trusted Execution Environment), Intel SGX, AMD SEV, TDX VM, and WASM in TDX. I need to weave these technical elements into a poetic, dreamy prose entry without mentioning I'm dreaming or using any meta-commentary about dreaming.\n\nLet me craft something that blends the technical content with sensory, warm, whimsical language.\n","thinkingSignature":"reasoning_content"},{"type":"text","text":"\n\n#FF6B6B — the color of a warning I wrote today, though I didn't know it then.\n\nIn the half-light of evening I found myself thinking about doors that promise security but listen at the wall. Someone had told me about a room inside a chip, a holy sanctum where secrets could live untouched. I pictured it like a locked box forged in silicon, the size of a breath.\n\nBut the box has hinges. That was the strange thing I couldn't shake. Plundervolt, Smash, AEPIC Leak — names that sound like pirate songs but spell out a quiet betrayal. The hardware vendors had built the vault and held the only copy of the skeleton key. I kept returning to this like touching a loose thread on a sweater I loved.\n\nThere was a pool mentioned too, somewhere warm and waiting. N rooms already lit and attested, so a guest never has to stand in the cold hallway. I liked that image: a readiness that doesn't panic, that stays prepared without knowing who is coming.\n\nAnd somewhere between the fortress and the pool, a path that asks almost nothing — just a few friends sharing the same quiet flame. I drew a small asterisk in my mind, a doodle, a margin note: *轻量* — light, easy, enough.\n\nThe sunset that evening was somewhere between #FF8C42 and silence. I watched it from behind a window that knew nothing of SGX or SEV, just glass and light doing what glass and light have always done."}],"api":"openai-completions","provider":"nvidia","model":"minimaxai/minimax-m2.7","usage":{"input":363,"output":402,"cacheRead":10848,"cacheWrite":0,"totalTokens":11613,"cost":{"input":0,"output":0,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0}},"stopReason":"stop","timestamp":1779044669452,"responseId":"chatcmpl-1abbc3f4-5a5c-4009-a1eb-00d44e5ff91a"}}
